00:39:47.420 --> 00:39:48.520
Oh, my gosh!

1014
00:39:48.660 --> 00:39:49.340
That's Brian!

1015
00:39:49.740 --> 00:39:50.980
That is Brian's voice.

1016
00:39:51.140 --> 00:39:51.520
That's not.

1017
00:39:51.600 --> 00:39:54.460
Because Kevin would have been like, yeah, it'll probably be me.

1018
00:39:54.460 --> 00:39:55.680
It'll probably be me.

1019
00:39:55.800 --> 00:39:55.980
Yeah.

1020
00:39:56.020 --> 00:39:56.860
That's a horrible Kevin.

1021
00:39:56.900 --> 00:39:58.860
We just really did not do that well.

1022
00:39:58.860 --> 00:39:59.280
Oh, my gosh.

1023
00:39:59.280 --> 00:40:00.660
I want to call Brian about it.

1024
00:40:00.780 --> 00:40:03.000
But when I watched it, I was like, wait a second.

1025
00:40:03.540 --> 00:40:04.700
It's like, that's Brian.

1026
00:40:05.220 --> 00:40:10.120
But I think in the pilot, we were still sort of like figuring out our characters and who they were.

1027
00:40:10.760 --> 00:40:12.800
However, I have to say, Angela.

1028
00:40:13.060 --> 00:40:13.240
What?

1029
00:40:13.420 --> 00:40:15.680
I went into the deleted scenes.

1030
00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:16.560
Oh, my God.

1031
00:40:16.560 --> 00:40:18.720
On the DVD, season one DVD.

1032
00:40:19.160 --> 00:40:19.440
And?

1033
00:40:19.540 --> 00:40:23.400
And there is, this is something we did on the pilot.

1034
00:40:23.720 --> 00:40:29.620
Some of it was an acting exercise where they called us each into the conference room separately.

1035
00:40:29.620 --> 00:40:36.380
And they just asked us unscripted lines about our characters and about our relationship to other characters.

1036
00:40:36.540 --> 00:40:37.420
I remember this.

1037
00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:38.040
It wasn't written.

1038
00:40:38.060 --> 00:40:38.760
It was not written.

1039
00:40:38.800 --> 00:40:39.860
We just improvised.

1040
00:40:39.860 --> 00:40:46.320
Oh, so this was sort of, I think, an exercise that Ken wanted to do that Greg and Ken came up with.

1041
00:40:46.460 --> 00:40:52.920
In addition to that thing where they filmed us all just working, they also filmed us being interviewed in character.

1042
00:40:53.200 --> 00:40:54.720
And I think Greg thought, this will be great.

1043
00:40:54.780 --> 00:40:57.400
Maybe I could use some of these little tidbits here and there.

1044
00:40:57.720 --> 00:41:01.700
Well, there is a series of interviews with each of the members of accounting.

1045
00:41:01.940 --> 00:41:02.540
Oh, my God.

1046
00:41:02.580 --> 00:41:06.580
Where you guys are all trash talking each other very subtly.

1047
00:41:07.360 --> 00:41:14.880
And Angela, you have this incredible deleted scene talking head where they ask you about Oscar.

1048
00:41:15.180 --> 00:41:17.000
Is this where I compare him to a stapler?

1049
00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:17.840
Yes.

1050
00:41:18.120 --> 00:41:20.100
Sam, can you pull that up so we can listen to that?

1051
00:41:20.260 --> 00:41:21.620
Oscar, how do I describe him?

1052
00:41:22.140 --> 00:41:23.800
He's like a stapler.

1053
00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:25.620
Do I need a stapler?

1054
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:26.160
Yes.

1055
00:41:26.900 --> 00:41:29.440
But I'm still the one that has to push it down.

1056
00:41:29.640 --> 00:41:30.180
I did.

1057
00:41:30.180 --> 00:41:34.980
I improvised that because I was trying to think of, like, what, like, how does Angela see Oscar?

1058
00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:39.680
And he's just, like, he's necessary, but he's a, he ends up being more work for her.

1059
00:41:39.820 --> 00:41:40.160
Yes.

1060
00:41:40.160 --> 00:41:40.920
But he's annoying.

1061
00:41:41.260 --> 00:41:48.260
What was so clear to me when I was watching them was this accounting dynamic had already started.

1062
00:41:48.560 --> 00:41:48.740
Yeah.

1063
00:41:48.740 --> 00:41:55.240
This little pod that you guys form, this little trio, it was there from the very beginning.

1064
00:41:55.780 --> 00:42:00.460
Also, I do have to point, fans, all of the deleted scenes are fantastic.

1065
00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:03.320
Rainn Wilson has some talking heads.

1066
00:42:03.320 --> 00:42:11.160
There is a long, extended, deleted scene-talking head of him talking to Ken Quapis, who played the documentarian for us.

1067
00:42:11.200 --> 00:42:16.260
He would ask us the questions, our director, all about where the boom microphone was.

1068
00:42:17.100 --> 00:42:20.680
Rainn, as Dwight, was very distracted by the boom.

1069
00:42:21.020 --> 00:42:21.680
Oh, my God.

1070
00:42:21.700 --> 00:42:24.200
And he was saying, I really need you to move that.

1071
00:42:24.480 --> 00:42:26.300
Ken says, we can put it in your blind spot.

1072
00:42:26.300 --> 00:42:28.280
And he says something like, I don't have a blind spot.

1073
00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:31.200
I've been trained, so it's especially distracting for me.

1074
00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:33.120
You need to understand that I'm highly trained.

1075
00:42:33.260 --> 00:42:40.480
And it's just this little, like, non-presentational conversation between Dwight and the documentarian about how to be mic'd.

1076
00:42:40.520 --> 00:42:41.640
I just want to say one thing.

1077
00:42:41.860 --> 00:42:46.300
So many great things that were established in the pilot that you go on to see for years to come.

1078
00:42:46.480 --> 00:42:49.500
Of course, one of the big ones is the Jim versus Dwight.

1079
00:42:49.500 --> 00:42:51.640
And, like, sort of their battle, right?

1080
00:42:51.760 --> 00:42:54.280
And the pranks that Jim is going to do on Dwight.

1081
00:42:54.420 --> 00:43:00.460
And I love that it just started out so simply with Dwight pushing all of Jim's papers back to his desk.

1082
00:43:00.480 --> 00:43:02.480
And then Jim making the pencil wall.

1083
00:43:03.020 --> 00:43:04.200
It's just ridiculous.

1084
00:43:04.740 --> 00:43:06.640
Well, that was borrowed from the British show.

1085
00:43:06.800 --> 00:43:08.940
In the British show, they have the same desk war.

1086
00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:12.320
But instead, the Jim character piles up a bunch of boxes.

1087
00:43:12.480 --> 00:43:14.840
He makes a box wall between the desks.

1088
00:43:15.340 --> 00:43:17.620
And we did that when we filmed the pilot.

1089
00:43:17.800 --> 00:43:19.980
We had Jim make a box wall.

1090
00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:24.160
And, in fact, you can see it in the background of conference room scenes.

1091
00:43:24.300 --> 00:43:27.260
You can see a bunch of boxes piled up on Jim's desk.

1092
00:43:27.340 --> 00:43:29.440
My lady, I'm going to go back and look.

1093
00:43:29.940 --> 00:43:36.460
Later, when we got picked up, we reshot that scene and turned it into a little pencil thing.

1094
00:43:36.620 --> 00:43:42.580
And you can also see that Rain's hair is a little bit different in the pencil scene compared to the rest of the pilot.

1095
00:43:42.700 --> 00:43:43.380
It's not as poofy.

1096
00:43:43.620 --> 00:43:44.220
That's right.

1097
00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:44.540
Yeah.

1098
00:43:44.540 --> 00:43:45.120
Exactly.

1099
00:43:45.520 --> 00:43:51.620
Rain, as Dwight, went through poofy hair phase, which looks like they used a little miniature, like, rolling brush to blow dry his hair.

1100
00:43:51.780 --> 00:43:54.620
And then he went through flat, parted-down-the-middle phase.

1101
00:43:54.800 --> 00:43:57.160
Well, Rain created the hairstyle for Dwight.

1102
00:43:57.220 --> 00:44:02.840
And he said before that it is based on the hairstyle that he wore when he was a 16-year-old boy.

1103
00:44:03.420 --> 00:44:05.460
And so he did his own hair for the pilot.

1104
00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:06.960
That makes me laugh.

1105
00:44:07.140 --> 00:44:08.820
I've seen those photos of Rain.

1106
00:44:09.080 --> 00:44:09.840
They're crazy.

1107
00:44:10.260 --> 00:44:11.720
You wore your own clothes in the pilot.

1108
00:44:11.760 --> 00:44:13.660
I wore my own clothes in the pilot.

1109
00:44:13.660 --> 00:44:14.280
All right.

1110
00:44:14.420 --> 00:44:22.580
So the last sort of thing I think we need to talk about is this big prank on Pam, quote-unquote, the scene where Michael fake fires her.

1111
00:44:22.580 --> 00:44:26.340
Well, he's so excited because Jim has had a very successful prank.

1112
00:44:26.560 --> 00:44:29.000
And Michael just, he wants to be in the spotlight.

1113
00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:30.260
He wants to be the funny guy.

1114
00:44:30.260 --> 00:44:34.680
So he's going to show off for Ryan the 10th, and he's going to fake fire Pam.

1115
00:44:35.060 --> 00:44:38.000
And it, of course, goes horribly wrong, and she ends up in tears.

1116
00:44:38.180 --> 00:44:42.380
And we shot that scene probably 30 times.

1117
00:44:42.580 --> 00:44:42.840
Wow.

1118
00:44:42.840 --> 00:44:48.320
And at the beginning of the scene, you can see everyone in the background kind of getting ready to leave for the day.

1119
00:44:49.440 --> 00:44:52.740
And all those people had to wait for hours.

1120
00:44:53.080 --> 00:44:56.580
They would have to start in the background, and then we would do this whole scene.

1121
00:44:56.620 --> 00:44:57.920
Oh, I know, Jenna.

1122
00:44:58.040 --> 00:44:58.500
I know.

1123
00:44:58.800 --> 00:44:59.760
I was there.

1124
00:44:59.940 --> 00:45:03.020
I had to grab my jacket, my coat, and my purse, put them down.

1125
00:45:03.120 --> 00:45:04.000
My coat and my purse.

1126
00:45:04.000 --> 00:45:11.340
I think of any scene in the entire history of The Office, this is the one that I've done the most because we did about 30 takes of it that day.

1127
00:45:11.420 --> 00:45:13.320
But it was also my audition scene.

1128
00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:15.620
This was one of my audition scenes.

1129
00:45:15.760 --> 00:45:19.440
And so I auditioned for months for this role.

1130
00:45:19.680 --> 00:45:24.220
I did that scene one time when I auditioned for the role of Pam, and I didn't get it.

1131
00:45:25.460 --> 00:45:28.580
This is such a crazy, crazy bit of trivia.

1132
00:45:28.600 --> 00:45:29.200
Yes, yes.

1133
00:45:29.320 --> 00:45:32.080
Your first audition for The Office was for the role of Pam.

1134
00:45:32.080 --> 00:45:35.440
It was for the role of Pam, and I wore a pink sweater.

1135
00:45:35.760 --> 00:45:36.080
What?

1136
00:45:36.240 --> 00:45:36.380
Yes.

1137
00:45:36.380 --> 00:45:37.440
We both had the same instinct.

1138
00:45:37.620 --> 00:45:38.700
Pam wears pink sweater.

1139
00:45:38.880 --> 00:45:45.400
I wore a pink sweater and my hair down, and I was told to look, you know, like not too fancy, so I didn't do too much with my hair and makeup.

1140
00:45:45.620 --> 00:45:50.280
And I went in, and I did the scene, and it was for a room full of people, the producers.

1141
00:45:50.760 --> 00:45:56.200
And when we got to the point where Michael fake fires you, and you start to cry, and you call him a jerk.

1142
00:45:56.420 --> 00:45:56.640
Yeah.

1143
00:45:57.100 --> 00:46:00.040
When I called him a jerk, everyone started to laugh.

1144
00:46:00.160 --> 00:46:01.880
And I thought, I did something wrong.

1145
00:46:02.360 --> 00:46:04.300
I don't think they're supposed to laugh at this moment.

1146
00:46:04.520 --> 00:46:12.600
And of course, like, Jenna, you were so brilliant because you brought such a vulnerability to Pam that even though this job sucks and she hates it, she needs it.

1147
00:46:12.740 --> 00:46:14.400
She needs this crappy job.

1148
00:46:14.500 --> 00:46:14.660
Yeah.

1149
00:46:14.660 --> 00:46:17.420
And you really felt her in that moment.

1150
00:46:17.600 --> 00:46:19.360
You just, my heart broke for her.

1151
00:46:19.780 --> 00:46:23.600
And when you call him a jerk, it's just like you're really wounded.

1152
00:46:23.640 --> 00:46:28.120
And it checks Michael in his place of like, that wasn't cool.

1153
00:46:28.280 --> 00:46:28.720
Right?

1154
00:46:28.720 --> 00:46:33.320
It's funny because this was a somewhat controversial scene about whether or not it should be included.

1155
00:46:33.520 --> 00:46:41.620
When Ricky and Steven were counseling Greg, I understand that they told him that he should consider cutting the scene.

1156
00:46:41.620 --> 00:46:48.820
Because they said that it's in their pilot and they felt like they always had to fight to come back from it.

1157
00:46:48.980 --> 00:46:52.020
That it made the boss a little too mean.

1158
00:46:52.020 --> 00:46:57.480
And so later they really leaned into his buffoonery.

1159
00:46:58.180 --> 00:47:00.000
But Greg fought to keep it in.

1160
00:47:00.120 --> 00:47:02.840
He thought, no, we're going to try it.

1161
00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:04.040
We're going to let her cry.

1162
00:47:04.200 --> 00:47:05.960
We're going to let Michael be mean to her.

1163
00:47:05.960 --> 00:47:13.680
Now, there was an alt line where I think that sometimes instead of saying you're a jerk, I said you're a sad little man.

1164
00:47:14.640 --> 00:47:16.840
And they said that's too harsh.

1165
00:47:17.700 --> 00:47:19.300
You can't come back from that.

1166
00:47:19.600 --> 00:47:20.560
That is harsh.

1167
00:47:20.780 --> 00:47:24.020
